# Files that are executed by a Linux kernel MUST keep LF endings, whatever the checkout host
# does. This repository is cloned on Windows machines with core.autocrlf=true; a CRLF checkout of
# a script with `#!/bin/sh` makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r",
# and the container fails at start with
#     exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# which names the script that plainly exists and says nothing about why. (.github/workflows/ci.yml
# in this tree is already CRLF, so the conversion demonstrably happens here.)
#
# docker/Dockerfile.apiserver strips CRs at build time as well, for a context that reached the
# daemon some other way. This is the fix at the source.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
